{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-20T19:04:27.499Z","data":{"text":"Task 4 complete. Summary:\n\n## What happened\n\nThe production implementation for `osq plan` already existed in the committed tree (`e51fa90`), and the task verify passed 3/3 before I started. I found no implementation gaps, so no changes were needed to `src/cli/plan.ts`, `src/cli/index.ts`, or `tests/fixtures/brief.md`.\n\nMy work was strengthening `tests/plan.test.ts` (in scope, `tests.modify: true`) so each acceptance line is genuinely proven rather than incidentally passed:\n\n- **Line 1 (ordering):** Added an `InspectingAdapter` that snapshots the filesystem *inside* `spawnInteractive`, proving the change folder and `brief.md` exist before the session opens. The old test only checked they existed afterward.\n- **Line 3 (PLANNER.md content):** Now asserts the prompt `startsWith` the real `PLANNER.md` content plus a distinctive managed-block line. The old assertion matched a fallback header, so it could pass even if PLANNER.md were absent.\n- **Line 4 (`-print`):** Captures both stdout and stderr, asserts no spawn, no creation logs on either stream, and that the folder/brief are still created. Added a CLI-level test driving `-print` through `createProgram`.\n- **Line 5 (resume):** Asserts exactly one change folder remains and `brief.md` is byte-identical after resume.\n- **Line 4/CLI:** Added a registration test for `plan <name>` with `--brief`/`--print`.\n\n## Deviations\n\nCommander 13.1.0 cannot register `-print` as a short flag, so the code uses `-p, --print` plus a `-print` → `--print` normalization in `index.ts`. I verified this works end-to-end (`-print` prints the prompt to stdout only, exit 0). Documented in the result file.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/plan.test.ts` → **5/5 pass**\n- `pnpm tsc --noEmit` → clean\n- `pnpm lint` → clean\n- `pnpm test` → **690/690 pass**\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/031-planner-in-osq/.run/results/4.md`."}}
